@lang en

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ito-credit-points-nouns`
IMPORT `ito-s33a-credit-point`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Income Tax Ordinance [New Version] — ss 34, 36 and 36A: the three personal
-- credit points that carry no condition beyond who the taxpayer is. Row IL-01.
--
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/income-tax-ordinance-new-version.he.wiki.txt
--   (sha256 b87f2cf4...b81b6; "line N" is a line of that file). Hebrew is
--   authoritative; quotations are rendered mechanically by render_source.py.
--
-- Each section is one sentence: "In computing the tax of <a person of this
-- kind>, <so many> credit points shall be taken into account." Each is
-- encoded twice over:
--   * `section N, as written, applies to` — the sentence's own limbs, nothing
--     else, so a reader can hold the Hebrew beside it;
--   * `section N applies to` — the same, with the two provisions OUTSIDE this
--     row that can change the answer for some people: s 48 (an order may
--     extend ss 34 and 36 to Area residents who are not Israeli citizens) and
--     s 48A (regulations may disapply the Chapter's credits to a foreign
--     worker). Neither is encoded, so where either could decide the case the
--     rule REFUSES, and only there.
-- A person to whom a section does not apply gets no points under it. That is
-- the law's own answer, an ordinary 0, not a refusal.
--
-- None of these is the person's TOTAL of credit points: ss 35, 37-40D, 44-46
-- and others add more (row IL-08), and s 41 and s 66 rework them for spouses
-- (rows IL-08 and IL-02). The aggregates below are named for exactly the
-- sections they add.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Part C, Chapter Three — credits under sections 34, 36 and 36A`

§§ `Reading the facts of the case`

-- Accessors over a Person. A body of persons is not an individual, so every
-- fact an individual carries is FALSE for it.

GIVEN p IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is an individual` p MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `an individual` i  THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a body of persons` THEN FALSE

GIVEN p IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person was an Israeli resident in the tax year` p MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `an individual` i  THEN i's `an Israeli resident in the tax year`
    WHEN `a body of persons` THEN FALSE

GIVEN p IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is a woman` p MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `an individual` i  THEN i's `a woman`
    WHEN `a body of persons` THEN FALSE

GIVEN p IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen` p MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `an individual` i  THEN i's `a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen`
    WHEN `a body of persons` THEN FALSE

GIVEN p IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is a foreign worker` p MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `an individual` i  THEN i's `a foreign worker`
    WHEN `a body of persons` THEN FALSE

§§ `Sections 48 and 48A — reached, not encoded`

-- line 1807: שר האוצר, באישור ועדת הכספים של הכנסת, רשאי לקבוע בצו כי הוראות סעיפים 34, 36 ו־37, כולן או מקצתן, יחולו ... גם לגבי תושבי אזור שאינם אזרחים ישראליים, כולם או חלקם, כאילו היו תושבי ישראל
-- The power has been exercised: the Wikisource note at line 1808 records
-- the Income Tax (Credits for Area Residents) Order 5755-1995, applying
-- ss 34, 36 and 37 to Area residents who are not Israeli citizens "as if
-- they were Israeli residents". The order is not in this row's source
-- bundle and s 48 is outside this row, so where it could decide the case —
-- a non-resident individual who is an Area resident and not an Israeli
-- citizen — the rule refuses. (s 48 does not name s 36A; see fork F1.)
@ref ITO s 48, lines 1806-1808 — not encoded in this row
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 48 and the order made under it are not encoded in this model` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 48 and the order made under it are not encoded in this model"

-- line 1811: שר האוצר רשאי לקבוע כי הוראות פרק זה לענין זיכויים, כולן או מקצתן, לא יחולו על עובד זר ... או שיחולו עליהם באופן חלקי
-- The power has been exercised: the Wikisource note at line 1812 records the
-- Income Tax (Credits for a Foreign Worker) Regulations 5775-2014. They can
-- only take credits away ("לא יחולו", "באופן חלקי"), so they matter only
-- where a section would otherwise give a foreign worker points; there the
-- rule refuses. Where the section gives nothing anyway, the answer stands.
@ref ITO s 48A, lines 1810-1812 — not encoded in this row
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 48A and the regulations made under it are not encoded in this model` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 48A and the regulations made under it are not encoded in this model"

§§ `Section 34 — Credit for an Israeli resident`
-- line 1569: סעיף 34: זיכוי לתושב ישראל
-- line 1570: בחישוב המס של יחיד שהיה תושב ישראל בשנת המס יובאו בחשבון שתי נקודות זיכוי.

@ref ITO s 34, line 1570
GIVEN p IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 34, as written, applies to` p MEANS
        "של יחיד" ... `the person is an individual` p
    AND "שהיה תושב ישראל בשנת המס" ... `the person was an Israeli resident in the tax year` p

@ref ITO s 34, line 1570; s 48, line 1807; s 48A, line 1811
GIVEN p IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 34 applies to` p MEANS
    BRANCH IF `section 34, as written, applies to` p AND `the person is a foreign worker` p
               THEN `section 48A and the regulations made under it are not encoded in this model`
           IF `section 34, as written, applies to` p
               THEN TRUE
           IF `the person is an individual` p AND `the person is a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen` p
               THEN `section 48 and the order made under it are not encoded in this model`
           OTHERWISE FALSE

-- "יובאו בחשבון שתי נקודות זיכוי" — two credit points shall be taken into account.
@ref ITO s 34, line 1570
GIVEN p IS A Person
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the credit points under section 34 for` p MEANS
    IF   `section 34 applies to` p
    THEN 2
    ELSE 0

§§ `Section 36 — Credit for travel to the place of earning`
-- line 1593: סעיף 36: זיכוי בעד נסיעה למקום ההשתכרות
-- line 1594: בחישוב המס של יחיד תושב ישראל תובא בחשבון 1⁄4 נקודת זיכוי כזיכוי נסיעה.
--
-- The heading speaks of travel to the place of earning; the sentence imposes
-- no condition of earning or travel. Encoded as the sentence reads (fork F2).
-- "יחיד תושב ישראל" carries no "in the tax year"; read as the same
-- residence-for-the-tax-year that s 34 names (fork F3).

@ref ITO s 36, line 1594
GIVEN p IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 36, as written, applies to` p MEANS
        "של יחיד" ... `the person is an individual` p
    AND "תושב ישראל" ... `the person was an Israeli resident in the tax year` p

@ref ITO s 36, line 1594; s 48, line 1807; s 48A, line 1811
GIVEN p IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 36 applies to` p MEANS
    BRANCH IF `section 36, as written, applies to` p AND `the person is a foreign worker` p
               THEN `section 48A and the regulations made under it are not encoded in this model`
           IF `section 36, as written, applies to` p
               THEN TRUE
           IF `the person is an individual` p AND `the person is a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen` p
               THEN `section 48 and the order made under it are not encoded in this model`
           OTHERWISE FALSE

-- "תובא בחשבון 1⁄4 נקודת זיכוי כזיכוי נסיעה" — a quarter of a credit point
-- shall be taken into account, as a travel credit.
@ref ITO s 36, line 1594
GIVEN p IS A Person
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the credit points under section 36 for` p MEANS
    IF   `section 36 applies to` p
    THEN 1/4
    ELSE 0

§§ `Section 36A — Credit for a woman`
-- line 1596: סעיף 36א: זיכוי לאשה
-- line 1597: בחישוב המס של אשה תובא בחשבון 1⁄2 נקודת זיכוי.
--
-- The sentence has one limb, "אשה". It does not say "תושב ישראל", as ss 34
-- and 36 beside it do, and s 48 does not list it among the sections it
-- extends to non-residents. Encoded as the sentence reads: residence is not
-- a condition (fork F1).

@ref ITO s 36A, line 1597
GIVEN p IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 36A, as written, applies to` p MEANS
    "של אשה" ... `the person is a woman` p

-- s 48 does not reach s 36A, so only s 48A can change the answer.
@ref ITO s 36A, line 1597; s 48A, line 1811
GIVEN p IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 36A applies to` p MEANS
    BRANCH IF `section 36A, as written, applies to` p AND `the person is a foreign worker` p
               THEN `section 48A and the regulations made under it are not encoded in this model`
           OTHERWISE `section 36A, as written, applies to` p

-- "תובא בחשבון 1⁄2 נקודת זיכוי" — half a credit point shall be taken into account.
@ref ITO s 36A, line 1597
GIVEN p IS A Person
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the credit points under section 36A for` p MEANS
    IF   `section 36A applies to` p
    THEN 1/2
    ELSE 0

§§ `Aggregates the Ordinance names`

-- line 4864: מסכום נקודות הזיכוי שעל פי סעיפים 34 ו־36
-- s 134A(2) (a power to exempt from filing a return, outside this row) names
-- this aggregate, so it is provided under that name.
@ref ITO ss 34 and 36, lines 1570 and 1594; named in s 134A(2), line 4864
GIVEN p IS A Person
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the credit points under sections 34 and 36 for` p MEANS
         `the credit points under section 34 for` p
    PLUS `the credit points under section 36 for` p

-- The whole of this row's slice. NOT the person's total credit points.
@ref ITO ss 34, 36 and 36A, lines 1570, 1594 and 1597
GIVEN p IS A Person
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A for` p MEANS
         `the credit points under section 34 for` p
    PLUS `the credit points under section 36 for` p
    PLUS `the credit points under section 36A for` p

-- The same points as an amount of money, at the year's indexed value of a
-- credit point (s 33A; the value is an input, see ito-s33a-credit-point.l4).
@export The amount in NIS of the credit points an Israeli taxpayer gets under Income Tax Ordinance ss 34, 36 and 36A alone (not their total credit points), given the indexed value of one credit point for the tax year
@ref ITO s 33A, line 1563; ss 34, 36 and 36A, lines 1570, 1594 and 1597
GIVEN p                               IS A Person  @desc the taxpayer: an individual (with residence, sex, Area-residence and foreign-worker facts) or a body of persons
      `the value of one credit point` IS A NUMBER  @desc NIS; the s 33A amount as indexed under s 120B for the tax year (2,904 for 2025 per the Israel Tax Authority)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount of the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A for` p `at a credit-point value of` `the value of one credit point` MEANS
    `the amount of` (`the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A for` p) `credit points at a credit-point value of` `the value of one credit point`
